whereabouts were unknown. If Hannah had still been alive, she would have since celebrated her 18th birthday and completed her A-level exams, moving on to pursue medical studies at university. On Friday, March 12, 2004, two days prior to the one-year anniversary of her murder, Hillary and Trevor Foster released a statement via the media which read, This continues to be the worst time in our lives. We miss Hannah terribly. The injustice of her death is intensified by the knowledge that her killer is still

